WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.268
-President Trump has been
holding

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.470
a lot of press briefings
lately,

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.338
but his rambling, nonsensical
responses

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:08.574
leave a lot of important
questions unanswered.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:10.710
So we decided to hold another
one right here, right now.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.079
Unfortunately, the rest of
the "Late Night" press corps

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.547
couldn't make it tonight because

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.916
they're still waiting on their
COVID test results.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:20.019
But President Trump is here,
and he's ready to go.

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.188
So without further ado,
it's time

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.824
for the "Late Night" White House
press briefing.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:32.665
♪♪

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.968
-Mr. President, Mr. President,
Mr. President, Mr. President.

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.638
Thank you, Seth Meyers,
"Late Night With Seth Meyers."

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.641
President Trump, what would you
say to reassure people

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.344
with pre-existing conditions
who are terrified

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.879
of catching the coronavirus?

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:50.849
-The stock market went up
358 points today.

00:00:50.849 --> 00:00:52.852
-And what would you say
to reassure the people

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.622
who have been fortunate enough
to avoid catching the virus

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.456
thus far?
-You'll have it very shortly.

00:00:57.456 --> 00:01:00.293
-How would you describe
the 2020 presidential race?

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.495
-Elderly.
It's especially elderly.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.364
-And what are you hoping
to see on November 3rd?

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:06.766
-A rigged election.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.301
-In your opinion, what is
the most egregious offense

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:11.036
the media can commit?

00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:12.572
-Not talking about me.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:16.009
-And what can you tell me about
that suit you're wearing?

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.610
-Covers a lot of territory.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.146
-Hey, tell us, when you
meet another world leader,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.648
how do you shake their hand?

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:26.386
-Very, very strongly and, uh,
very, very hard.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.821
-How many states do you
think you'll carry

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.189
in the election?

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.325
-40, 50, 60, and maybe even 70.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.993
-Well, 70, that's something.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.129
You don't seem to have as many
friends as you used to.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.897
Why is that?
-They're being arrested,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.198
they're being put in jail.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.200
And that's why you see
those numbers going down.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.870
-How would you describe
Switzerland's flag?

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.372
-It's a big plus.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:51.210
-If Chris Cuomo competed
at the Olympics,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.346
what kind of medal
do you think he'd win?

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.980
-Fake media gold.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.249
-What are your pants like
as you lie your way through

00:01:57.249 --> 00:01:58.517
these press briefings?

00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:00.687
-Pretty much on fire.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.521
-President Trump,
a geography question.

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:05.057
How frackin' big is Texas?

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:06.693
-That's a big fracking state.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.794
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.562
What's your youngest
daughter's name?

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:10.563
-Jennifer.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.964
-No, actually, it's Tiffany.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.000
The answer you were looking for
was Tiffany.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:18.738
Okay.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.139
How'd you do on your S.A.T.s?

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.808
-Half a million incorrect.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.876
-What do you call a sandwich

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.978
on a hamburger bun

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:30.683
made with ground beef, onions,
tomato sauce, and Ambien?

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.885
-Sleepy Joe.

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:37.056
-When your son Eric
was conceived,

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.525
which of your sperm
fertilized the egg?

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.160
-The slowest, weakest,
and worst.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.362
-What was Charles Barkley's
most impressive skill

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:44.797
on the basketball court?

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.600
-Rebounding with strength like
nobody thought possible.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.602
-The round mound to rebound.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.772
Is there anything you'd like to
say to all the chairs

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.440
you've sat on over the years?

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.742
-I want to thank them
for their strength,

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.010
their bravery.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.179
-What's your favorite part

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.881
of a Michael Bay movie?

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.816
-An automobile boom.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.118
-Like an explosion?

00:03:06.118 --> 00:03:08.754
What do you need in order
to fix your brain?

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:11.391
-The largest and most advanced
operation of its kind

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:14.092
anywhere in the world
and anywhere in history.

00:03:14.092 --> 00:03:16.829
-Is it true that you're
writing a Broadway musical?

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.831
-A lot of people are
going to be very happy

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.967
when they see some
of the numbers.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.269
-Yeah, I mean,
I can't wait for that.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.605
Here's a question
about romance.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:28.674
What did Melania say the first
time she saw you naked?

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:30.643
-Gee, I don't know exactly
what that is.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:31.844
-Oh.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:34.981
Hey, I'm looking
to score a little --

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.115
[ Inhales ]

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.184
You know anyone I should
talk to about that?

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:41.653
-Chuck Schumer
and Nancy Pelosi are holding.

00:03:41.653 --> 00:03:44.591
-Wow! Chuck and Nancy.
Who would have thought?

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:47.794
Hey, why did we never get to see
Wilson on "Home Improvement"?

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.495
-The fencing -- especially
the new fencing

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.430
that they put up is
very powerful.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.999
-Uh-huh. Com--

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:57.236
Complete this famous
song lyric --

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.705
♪ A, B, C, D, E, F, G... ♪

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:01.708
-HHS and CDC.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:04.243
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.511
Ah!

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.046
What's your favorite
John Carpenter movie?

00:04:08.046 --> 00:04:09.715
-The fog was so great.

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:14.186
-Yeah, it is, but what is,
uh, that one,

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:15.955
you know, it takes
place in Antarctica?

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:18.024
You know, Kurt Russell?

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.992
-That's the thing.
-"The Thing"!

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:21.194
That's right.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.230
What would happen
if I opened up, like,

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.299
a hundred tabs in Safari?

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:29.435
-You will have a crash like
you've never seen before.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.471
-What country is your wife
Melania from?

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.705
-The Netherlands.
-Nope.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.340
-Sweden.
-Nope.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.441
-Belgium.
-Nope.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.709
-Estonia?
-Nope.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.746
-Slovakia?
-Neh, I'll give it to you.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.050
What's the highest number
you can count to?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.219
-A number that nobody's ever
heard of before.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:50.022
-Why did you stop wearing
an adult diaper?

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:52.191
-Don't like to put it on
because it shows.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.993
-Looks like we have time
for one more question.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:56.095
What did Melania say to you
on your birthday?

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.663
-We could do it through
teleconference.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:00.333
-Well, it looks like
we're out of time.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.601
So on behalf of the rest of

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.202
the "Late Night" press corps,
have a good night.

